<DiseasePage
  title="IgA Nephropathy"
  description="IgA Nephropathy (Berger's Disease) is one of the most common forms of kidney disease worldwide, and one of the least discussed."
  fullName="IgA Nephropathy (Berger's Disease)"
  whatItIs="IgA Nephropathy occurs when an antibody called immunoglobulin A builds up in the kidneys, causing inflammation that can gradually damage the kidneys' filtering ability. It often goes undetected for years, sometimes discovered only after blood or protein shows up in routine urine tests."
  whoItAffects="IgA Nephropathy affects people across every racial and ethnic background, making it an important part of The Jentosy Project's education work — a reminder that rare kidney disease is not only a story about any one community, even as some conditions like FSGS and APOL1-related disease disproportionately affect Black and Brown communities."
  whyItMatters="Because IgA Nephropathy is under-discussed and slow to diagnose, education and early awareness — the same tools The Jentosy Project uses for FSGS and APOL1-related disease — are just as critical here."
/>
